@* Ported from Index.ascx + .ascx.cs + .ascx.designer.cs.

   ⚠ CONTENT-FREE BY ORIGIN - this is a VERIFIED FACT, not an omission. The `.ascx` file
   contained ONLY the license comment and the <%@ Control %> directive (no placeholder, no
   markup), its `.ascx.designer.cs` declared NO fields at all, and its `OnControlLoad` body
   was ALREADY EMPTY. The legacy screen therefore rendered an empty region; emitting markup
   here would ADD a screen the module never had, and inventing a <Scrud> would mean guessing
   a table/view and would newly expose a table through a CRUD form.

   Beyond that, the whole behaviour is the base class's: Log.Verbose("{Control} initialized.")
   plus CheckAccessLevelAsync + CheckTransactionPostingStatusAsync, which MixERPUserControl
   runs for every control.

   The original declared no OverridePath, MasterPageId, RemoveTheme, IsLandingPage or
   IsRestrictedMode override, no AccessLevel override and implemented no ITransaction. *@

@inherits MixERP.Net.Framework.Controls.MixERPUserControl

@code {
    /// <summary>
    ///     MixERPUserControlBase.OnControlLoad is abstract, so every ported control must
    ///     declare it. The legacy body was ALREADY EMPTY (see the header), so an empty body
    ///     here is the base-class contract being satisfied, not a stub.
    /// </summary>
    public override void OnControlLoad(object sender, EventArgs e)
    {
    }
}
